\begin{abstract}
This research paper explores the application of the CRISP-DM methodology to the online retail dataset for customer segmentation. Each step of the CRISP-DM process is explained in detail, accompanied by relevant Python code. This structured approach provides insights into data preparation, modeling, and evaluation techniques. The findings from clustering highlight distinct customer segments, which businesses can leverage for marketing and decision-making strategies.
\end{abstract}

\section{Introduction}
The CRISP-DM (Cross-Industry Standard Process for Data Mining) methodology is widely adopted in data science due to its structured approach to data mining projects. This paper applies CRISP-DM to an online retail dataset, analyzing customer behaviors and segmenting them using K-Means clustering. The dataset consists of transactional data, including information about invoices, quantities, and prices, which will be used to develop a model for customer segmentation.

\section{Methodology: CRISP-DM Process with Code}
This section describes the CRISP-DM steps applied to the online retail dataset, along with Python code snippets for each step.

\subsection{Step 1: Business Understanding}
\textbf{Goal}: Analyze the purchase behavior of customers to identify patterns, such as top-selling products or frequent buyers.

\textbf{Objective}: Develop customer segmentation and product recommendation systems to increase sales and improve marketing strategies.

